it looks much like a regular night in a  regular pub but this where the spoons in  Twickenham is doing its bit to save our  oceans it swapped all its plastic straws  for paper wonders and next year every  business will have to go even further  all plastic straws and plastic starers  and cotton buns to be banned by April  2020 introducing the ban Environment  Secretary Michael Gove said urgent and  decisive action is needed to tackle  plastic pollution and protect our  environment these items are often used  for just a few minutes but take hundreds  of years to break down ending up in our  seas and oceans and harming precious  marine life so today I'm taking action  to turn the tide on plastic pollution  and ensure we leave our environment in a  better State for future generations this  now iconic image has come to represent  nature's losing battle against  single-use plastic it's prompted the  government to act but environment  charities say it's still not enough we  know that these three items do turn up  on our beaches they're normally in the  top 10 most commonly found items on  beaches but it is just three items there  is a lot more kinds of plastic pollution  out there we have plastic coming from  our clothing it's even in paint from the  tires on our cars you know plastic is  everywhere so we need a lot more action  from the government skies ocean rescue  campaign has been instrumental in  drawing attention to the plastic  poisoning our seas the company's chief  executive Jeremy Derek welcomed the  government's decisions he said  single-use plastic is a disease of our  own making we're working hard to get rid  of it and completely agree with Michael  Gove that urgent and decisive action is  needed it's estimated that we use up to  4.7 billion yes  billion plastic straws in England every  year and even though there are so many  alternatives available like metal or  glass or paper 95% of all straws in use  right now are still made from plastic  but that will now change awareness of  the issue is driving consumer behaviour  somebody gives me one at a bar I'll say  please Stowe but then they'll throw it  away if they put it in your dream  they'll just throw it away so it's good  replace it with paper you see the  protests in London even a month ago  people are stepping up and asking what  why is this can we do anything to  improve something as small as a straw  you know we can all do our part and it  makes a big difference in you we're only  just beginning to understand how much  damage single-use plastic is doing to  our planet but the warnings it seems are  finally being heeded and not before time  now she's Joshi Sky News
 

